{%- comment -%}
  A source marker: the small link after a claim saying where the claim came from. `cite_date` is
  optional by rule -- a dated source carries its date, a living document carries none, because a
  date on one would be a claim that is not true. All three names are cleared on exit (Liquid
  `assign` is global, see cratecard.liquid), which is what stops a dateless marker inheriting the
  date above it. A page using this opens by assigning the three "": Liquid errors on an unassigned
  name.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign cite_url_len = cite_url | size -%}
{%- assign cite_src_len = cite_src | size -%}
{%- assign cite_date_len = cite_date | size -%}
{%- if cite_url_len > 0 and cite_src_len > 0 -%}
<a class="cite" href="{{ cite_url | escape }}">{{ cite_src | escape }}{% if cite_date_len > 0 %}, {{ cite_date | escape }}{% endif %}&#160;<span class="cite-mark" aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
{%- else -%}
<strong class="cite-missing">[no source]</strong>
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign cite_url = "" -%}{%- assign cite_src = "" -%}{%- assign cite_date = "" -%}
